#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110337 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110564 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b903c40f-a2e5-5084-9c10-b2d33f423f1e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean"}] :question/id #uuid "9662033b-2a3a-5d80-91ad-ed542898b80b" :question/math-academy-id "e-14544" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X \\sim N(\\mu, 6^2)$ with $P(X > 4) = 0.1841,$ find $\\mu.$\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.00 \\,$ | $\\, 0.01 \\,$ | $\\, 0.02 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 0.7 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7580 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7611 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7642 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.8 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7881 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7910 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7939 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.9 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8159 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8186 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8212 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 4) & =1-P(X>4) \\\\  & =1-0.1841 \\\\  & =0.8159\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 4) & =0.8159 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{4-\\mu }{6}) & =0.8159 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{4-\\mu }{6}) & =0.8159 \\\\ \\frac{4-\\mu }{6} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.8159)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\Phi(0.90) = 0.8159 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad \\Phi^{-1}( 0.8159) = 0.90.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4-\\mu }{6} & =0.90 \\\\ 4-\\mu  & =5.4 \\\\ \\mu  & =-1.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110338 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110565 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "765f5ee4-b683-5c14-8e99-32241c029f39" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Variance or Standard Deviation"}] :question/id #uuid "35cc4c4c-79fb-5ae2-94e0-79f007af832b" :question/math-academy-id "e-14545" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X\\sim N(2.5, \\sigma^2)$ and $P(X \\geq 3) = 0.4013,$ find $\\sigma^2.$\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.03 \\,$ | $\\, 0.04 \\,$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 0.2 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5910 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5948 \\,$ | $\\, 0.5987 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.3 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6293 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6331 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6368 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.4 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6664 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6700 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6736 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =1-P(X\\ge 3) \\\\  & =1-0.4013 \\\\  & =0.5987\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =0.5987 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{3-2.5}{\\sigma }) & =0.5987 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{0.5}{\\sigma }) & =0.5987 \\\\ \\frac{0.5}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.5987)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\Phi(0.25) = 0.5987 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad \\Phi^{-1}( 0.5987) = 0.25.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{0.5}{\\sigma } & =0.25 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{0.5}{0.25} \\\\ \\sigma  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2}={2}^{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110339 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110566 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2bd470f-5459-5860-94cd-4ce9e6b70642" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Parameter Using Symmetry When the Mean Is Zero"}] :question/id #uuid "2a8633b4-f937-57e3-899d-c3176f07a48f" :question/math-academy-id "e-14546" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X \\sim N(0, \\sigma^2)$ is a normal random variable with $P(-3.18 <        X <        3.18) = 0.4038,$ find $\\sigma.$\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.02 \\,$ | $\\, 0.03 \\,$ | $\\, 0.04 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 0.4 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6628 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6664 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6700 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6985 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7019 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7054 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.6 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7324 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7357 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7389 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-3.18<X<3.18) & =0.4038 \\\\ 2P(0<X<3.18) & =0.4038 \\\\ P(0<X<3.18) & =0.2019 \\\\ P(X<3.18)-P(X<0) & =0.2019 \\\\ P(X<3.18)-0.5 & =0.2019 \\\\ P(X<3.18) & =0.7019 \\\\ P(X\\le 3.18) & =0.7019\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3.18) & =0.7019 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{3.18-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.7019 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{3.18}{\\sigma }) & =0.7019 \\\\ \\frac{3.18}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.7019)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\Phi(0.53) = 0.7019 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad \\Phi^{-1}( 0.7019) = 0.53.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3.18}{\\sigma } & =0.53 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{3.18}{0.53} \\\\ \\sigma  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110340 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110567 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45c41284-7cb9-5581-9b8f-5bbfce5aad0c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Parameter Using Symmetry When the Mean Is Nonzero"}] :question/id #uuid "5eb435ff-ef12-5f18-89d6-4ac163fae344" :question/math-academy-id "e-14548" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X \\sim N(\\mu, 2^2)$ is a normal random variable with $P( -4\\mu<             X <        6\\mu) = 0.6528,$ find $\\mu$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.03 \\,$ | $\\, 0.04 \\,$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 0.7 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7673 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7704 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7734 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.8 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7967 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7995 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8023 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.9 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8238 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8264 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8289 \\,$ |\n\n*Hint: Note that the interval $-4\\mu<             X <        6\\mu$ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu.$*" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can write the given probability as\n\n$$\nP(\\mu -5\\mu <     X <     \\mu +5\\mu) = 0.6528,\n$$\n\nwhich tells us that the interval $-4\\mu<             X <       6\\mu$ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu.$\n\nFirst, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mu -5\\mu <X<\\mu +5\\mu ) & =0.6528 \\\\ 2P(\\mu <X<\\mu +5\\mu ) & =0.6528 \\\\ P(\\mu <X<\\mu +5\\mu ) & =0.3264 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +5\\mu )-P(X<\\mu ) & =0.3264 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +5\\mu )-0.5 & =0.3264 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +5\\mu ) & =0.8264 \\\\ P(X\\le 6\\mu ) & =0.8264\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 6\\mu ) & =0.8264 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{6\\mu -\\mu }{2}) & =0.8264 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{5\\mu }{2}) & =0.8264 \\\\ \\frac{5\\mu }{2} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.8264)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\Phi(0.94) = 0.8264 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad \\Phi^{-1}( 0.8264) = 0.94.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5\\mu }{2} & =0.94 \\\\ 5\\mu  & =1.88 \\\\ \\mu  & ≈0.38\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110564 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b903c40f-a2e5-5084-9c10-b2d33f423f1e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53d6307a-364e-5b45-a243-85e1a8f8cc2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53d6307a-364e-5b45-a243-85e1a8f8cc2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418290} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d90d523-31e1-5f0f-8efe-27bdddda62ad" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b07a943e-feb9-5e5c-823f-0048a8326fe6" :question/math-academy-id "q-340851" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(\\mu ,{4}^{2})$ with $P(X\\ge 3)=0.3446,$ find $\\mu .$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6179\\,$ | $\\,0.6217\\,$ | $\\,0.6255\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6554\\,$ | $\\,0.6591\\,$ | $\\,0.6628\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.6915\\,$ | $\\,0.6950\\,$ | $\\,0.6985\\,$ |\n\n$\\mu =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =P(X<3) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\ge 3) \\\\  & =1-0.3446 \\\\  & =0.6554\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =0.6554 \\\\ P\\,(Z\\le \\frac{3-\\mu }{4}) & =0.6554 \\\\ Φ\\,(\\frac{3-\\mu }{4}) & =0.6554 \\\\ \\frac{3-\\mu }{4} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.6554)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have \n\n$$\nΦ(0.40)=0.6554\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.6554)=0.40.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3-\\mu }{4} & =0.40 \\\\ 3-\\mu  & =1.60 \\\\ \\mu  & =1.40.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317165 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110565 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "765f5ee4-b683-5c14-8e99-32241c029f39" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Variance or Standard Deviation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66a8e441-b6b2-591b-944b-3cfddb0ac398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66a8e441-b6b2-591b-944b-3cfddb0ac398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315690} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2534596-9656-56a2-a31c-8adf543ca897" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4a054739-7d5f-59e4-b190-1f466818f897" :question/math-academy-id "q-341655" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(3,{\\sigma }^{2})$ and $P(X\\ge 1)=0.8413,$ use the table to find $\\sigma .$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1587\\,$ | $\\,0.1562\\,$ | $\\,0.1539\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1841\\,$ | $\\,0.1814\\,$ | $\\,0.1788\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.2119\\,$ | $\\,0.2090\\,$ | $\\,0.2061\\,$ |\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 1) & =P(X<1) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\ge 1) \\\\  & =1-0.8413 \\\\  & =0.1587\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 1) & =0.1587 \\\\ P\\,(Z\\le \\frac{1-3}{\\sigma }) & =0.1587 \\\\ Φ\\,(-\\frac{2}{\\sigma }) & =0.1587 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.1587)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.00)=0.1587\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.1587)=-1.00.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sigma } & =-1 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418316 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110566 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2bd470f-5459-5860-94cd-4ce9e6b70642" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Parameter Using Symmetry When the Mean Is Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d6f0a73-e2e0-5875-93f7-c3a9c8822865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d6f0a73-e2e0-5875-93f7-c3a9c8822865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418294} :answer-field/id #uuid "69166d64-5e97-5c32-8220-3b2a1f609032" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7317b079-775e-5316-a7ce-180fb3a0e8c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-341988" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(0,{\\sigma }^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(-1.5<X<1.5)=0.3472,$ use the table to find $\\sigma ,$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6331\\,$ | $\\,0.6368\\,$ | $\\,0.6406\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6700\\,$ | $\\,0.6736\\,$ | $\\,0.6772\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.7054\\,$ | $\\,0.7088\\,$ | $\\,0.7123\\,$ |\n\n$\\sigma ≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.5<X<1.5) & =0.3472 \\\\ 2P(0<X<1.5) & =0.3472 \\\\ P(0<X<1.5) & =0.1736 \\\\ P(X<1.5)-P(X<0) & =0.1736 \\\\ P(X<1.5)-0.5 & =0.1736 \\\\ P(X<1.5) & =0.6736 \\\\ P(X\\le 1.5) & =0.6736\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 1.5) & =0.6736 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{1.5-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.6736 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{1.5}{\\sigma }) & =0.6736 \\\\ \\frac{1.5}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.6736)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.45)=0.6736\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.6736)=0.45.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1.5}{\\sigma } & =0.45 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{1.5}{0.45} \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈3.33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418315 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110566 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2bd470f-5459-5860-94cd-4ce9e6b70642" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Parameter Using Symmetry When the Mean Is Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cdaf6c6-dec3-5b38-a91c-2be375299096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cdaf6c6-dec3-5b38-a91c-2be375299096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418297} :answer-field/id #uuid "0824e9dc-c8d0-5712-a1a3-cb7ecbf153de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4375ac91-f4dd-57cf-abab-b28e66baa865" :question/math-academy-id "q-342034" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(0,{\\sigma }^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(|X|<3)=0.5468,$ find ${\\sigma }^{2}.$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ | $\\,0.7764\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7995\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ | $\\,0.8051\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8264\\,$ | $\\,0.8289\\,$ | $\\,0.8315\\,$ |\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given probability as\n\n$$\nP(|X|<3)=P(-3<X<3).\n$$\n\nThen, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-3<X<3) & =0.5468 \\\\ 2P(0<X<3) & =0.5468 \\\\ P(0<X<3) & =0.2734 \\\\ P(X<3)-P(X<0) & =0.2734 \\\\ P(X<3)-0.5 & =0.2734 \\\\ P(X<3) & =0.7734 \\\\ P(X\\le 3) & =0.7734\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =0.7734 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{3-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.7734 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{3}{\\sigma }) & =0.7734 \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.7734)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.75)=0.7734\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.7734)=0.75.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & =0.75 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{3}{0.75} \\\\ \\sigma  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =(4)^{2}=16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110564 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b903c40f-a2e5-5084-9c10-b2d33f423f1e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e523356-51e6-5eb9-8b16-754f02547625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418288} {:answer/id #uuid "5894f257-4ebc-5d56-a70d-cf0e5f88980b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418292} {:answer/id #uuid "5cefab71-1972-502d-b0e9-4eeba025fe95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418293} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7c4b24-62e9-5b3c-92b0-6a9e6302154f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418299} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d35c5e-62bc-5eec-b8a3-467f34a66e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e523356-51e6-5eb9-8b16-754f02547625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418288} :answer-field/id #uuid "a58e5b87-4733-54fd-a5a6-2ec4834dc8c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f740b39-58c8-58b2-9755-cce906b6c35a" :question/math-academy-id "q-94826" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(\\mu ,{4}^{2})$ with $P(X<2.5)=0.7881,$ find $\\mu .$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7257\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | $\\,0.7324\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2.5)=0.7881\\,⇒\\,P(X\\le 2.5)=0.7881\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2.5) & =0.7881 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{2.5-\\mu }{4}) & =0.7881 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{2.5-\\mu }{4}) & =0.7881 \\\\ \\frac{2.5-\\mu }{4} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.7881)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.80)=0.7881\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.7881)=0.80.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2.5-\\mu }{4} & =0.80 \\\\ 2.5-\\mu  & =3.2 \\\\ \\mu  & =-0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110565 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "765f5ee4-b683-5c14-8e99-32241c029f39" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Variance or Standard Deviation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c4717ce-46ec-5dfd-a87b-f3dbc1bd41c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418284} {:answer/id #uuid "4e35a48b-83ad-5a61-a3f1-7f195f1064b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418289} {:answer/id #uuid "53fe27ad-e859-55d8-9328-3819e6132d39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418291} {:answer/id #uuid "dd8135e4-0878-5169-b0ef-52cf2b36e46a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418301} {:answer/id #uuid "e35e3297-c505-59cf-87e9-2b40589a0852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e35a48b-83ad-5a61-a3f1-7f195f1064b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418289} :answer-field/id #uuid "fad179a2-756e-591e-8afb-194232c3b6f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12a69b61-bda4-5cdc-b9c6-93090eb9484f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94833" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(2,{\\sigma }^{2})$ and $P(X<-1)=0.3783,$ find $\\sigma ,$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3446\\,$ | $\\,0.3409\\,$ | $\\,0.3372\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3821\\,$ | $\\,0.3783\\,$ | $\\,0.3745\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.4207\\,$ | $\\,0.4168\\,$ | $\\,0.4129\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<-1)=0.3783\\,⇒\\,P(X\\le -1)=0.3783\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -1) & =0.3783 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{-1-2}{\\sigma }) & =0.3783 \\\\ Φ(-\\frac{3}{\\sigma }) & =0.3783 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.3783)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-0.31)=0.3783\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.3783)=-0.31.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & =-0.31 \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈9.68\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110567 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45c41284-7cb9-5581-9b8f-5bbfce5aad0c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Parameter Using Symmetry When the Mean Is Nonzero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0900ee31-7fc8-5a71-bfb0-567ce40867a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418283} {:answer/id #uuid "2c678ed7-d187-5b4d-b65e-df460c846e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418286} {:answer/id #uuid "929c9f87-8068-54c6-a062-0aad2ba05db7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418296} {:answer/id #uuid "c77996be-b841-5a9e-9afd-b3001a00c48c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418298} {:answer/id #uuid "fa154a6e-7b02-5897-b84b-0b4cfd53f21b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.74" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa154a6e-7b02-5897-b84b-0b4cfd53f21b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.74" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418305} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b3114c1-4daa-5e9a-8186-cd37d952aa3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02f6c3de-17f2-58af-afa6-5936538a62e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-94875" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(\\mu ,{3}^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(-0.7\\mu <X<2.7\\mu )=0.3256,$ find $\\mu $ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6217\\,$ | $\\,0.6255\\,$ | $\\,0.6293\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6591\\,$ | $\\,0.6628\\,$ | $\\,0.6664\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.6950\\,$ | $\\,0.6985\\,$ | $\\,0.7019\\,$ |\n\n*Hint: Note that the interval $-0.7\\mu <X<2.7\\mu $ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu .$*" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Note that we can write the given probability as\n\n$$\nP(\\mu -1.7\\mu <X<\\mu +1.7\\mu )=0.3256,\n$$\n\nwhich tells us that the interval $-0.7\\mu <X<2.7\\mu $ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu .$\n\nFirst, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mu -1.7\\mu <X<\\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.3256 \\\\ 2P(\\mu <X<\\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.3256 \\\\ P(\\mu <X<\\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.1628 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +1.7\\mu )-P(X<\\mu ) & =0.1628 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +1.7\\mu )-0.5 & =0.1628 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.6628 \\\\ P(X\\le \\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.6628 \\\\ P(X\\le 2.7\\mu ) & =0.6628\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2.7\\mu ) & =0.6628 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{2.7\\mu -\\mu }{3}) & =0.6628 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{1.7\\mu }{3}) & =0.6628 \\\\ \\frac{1.7\\mu }{3} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.6628)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.42)=0.6628\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.6628)=0.42.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1.7\\mu }{3} & =0.42 \\\\ 1.7\\mu  & =1.26 \\\\ \\mu  & ≈0.741\\,18 \\\\ \\mu  & ≈0.74.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110567 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45c41284-7cb9-5581-9b8f-5bbfce5aad0c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Parameter Using Symmetry When the Mean Is Nonzero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29c5beaa-2bd5-5a17-8ed7-0f68efb5d37f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.91" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418285} {:answer/id #uuid "37635532-f28a-53e6-ae9d-3b79e5b093b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418287} {:answer/id #uuid "6d43d3be-0f5b-5f12-af73-e68463fd21f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418295} {:answer/id #uuid "d88c6cd0-f17d-5079-9478-4d437c156ca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418300} {:answer/id #uuid "f6c68472-5317-5646-8c48-47295237b963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37635532-f28a-53e6-ae9d-3b79e5b093b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418287} :answer-field/id #uuid "e61ff356-8ad3-5164-a0c6-b21e9a847a8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418311}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "237d3289-35f7-5376-a92f-b552192446e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-94890" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(\\mu ,{5}^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(-0.8\\mu <X<2.8\\mu )=0.7458,$ find $\\mu ,$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8485\\,$ | $\\,0.8508\\,$ | $\\,0.8531\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8708\\,$ | $\\,0.8729\\,$ | $\\,0.8749\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8907\\,$ | $\\,0.8925\\,$ | $\\,0.8944\\,$ |\n\n*Hint: Note that the interval $-0.8\\mu <X<2.8\\mu $ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu .$*" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can write the given probability as\n\n$$\nP(\\mu -1.8\\mu <X<\\mu +1.8\\mu )=0.7458,\n$$\n\nwhich tells us that the interval $-0.8\\mu <X<2.8\\mu $ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu .$\n\nFirst, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mu -1.8\\mu <X<\\mu +1.8\\mu ) & =0.7458 \\\\ 2P(\\mu <X<\\mu +1.8\\mu ) & =0.7458 \\\\ P(\\mu <X<2.8\\mu ) & =0.3729 \\\\ P(X<2.8\\mu )-P(X<\\mu ) & =0.3729 \\\\ P(X<2.8\\mu )-0.5 & =0.3729 \\\\ P(X<2.8\\mu ) & =0.8729 \\\\ P(X\\le 2.8\\mu ) & =0.8729\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2.8\\mu ) & =0.8729 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{2.8\\mu -\\mu }{5}) & =0.8729 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{1.8\\mu }{5}) & =0.8729 \\\\ \\frac{1.8\\mu }{5} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.8729)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(1.14)=0.8729\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.8729)=1.14.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1.8\\mu }{5} & =1.14 \\\\ 1.8\\mu  & =5.7 \\\\ \\mu  & ≈3.166\\,67 \\\\ \\mu  & ≈3.17.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
